  "id": "Compound::DB00595 - Gene::9356",
  "verbalization": "Oxytetracycline is shown to bind to Slc22a11 and Slc22a7, both of which are involved in organic anion transport. This binding likely leads to the activation of Slc22a6, as these transporters are part of the same functional pathway. The evidence suggests that Oxytetracycline may modulate the activity of Slc22a6 through its interaction with Slc22a11 and Slc22a7, which are involved in the transport of organic anions across cellular membranes. The final scores from the paths indicate a moderate level of confidence in this relationship, though the exact mechanism of how Oxytetracycline influences Slc22a6 remains to be fully elucidated. The observed interactions suggest a potential role for Oxytetracycline in regulating the transport of organic anions, possibly through the modulation of Slc22a6 activity.",
